  "goodToKnow": "Der Brennstoff is fuel that's burned for heat or energy: Holz, Kohle, Heizöl, Gas; fossile Brennstoffe are fossil fuels. Fuel for engines is usually der Kraftstoff or der Treibstoff. Die Brennstoffzelle is a fuel cell. Since 2021 Germany has a national CO₂ price on heating and transport fuels under the Brennstoffemissionshandelsgesetz. Plural: die Brennstoffe."
